# Subagent Routing Mandate (Parent Agent)

The **parent agent** (main session) orchestrates; **specialist subagents** implement.
Do not substitute inline multi-file work for the pipeline in `.cursor/agents/`.

## Auto-intent (user should NOT need slash commands)

Map natural language to the same workflows as `.cursor/commands/*`. Slash commands
(`/deliver`, `/multitask-slices`, `/deploy-queue`, `/verify-done`) are **optional
shortcuts only** — if the user states the goal in plain Chinese/English, **execute
the matching workflow immediately** without asking them to type a slash command.

| User intent (examples) | Auto workflow | First action |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 做功能 / 修 bug / 交付 / 按管线做 / implement / deliver / “帮我把…做完” | **deliver** | `Task(delivery-orchestrator)` → stages 0–13 (+14 verifier when claiming Done); **one slice only** |
| 并行 / 同时做几件事 / 多切片 / multitask / 几个 worktree | **serial-queue** (default) | **Refuse fan-out.** Queue slices 1-by-1 via `deliver`. Only if user says `force-parallel` / `强制并行` → legacy multitask (cap ≤2 writers, queued Docker) |
| 部署 / 重启栈 / deploy / 队列状态 / 验收环境 | **deploy-queue** | `Task(build-deploy-agent)` → `docker-deploy-queue.ps1` (`-Status` / `-SkipBuild` as asked) |
| 验收 / 是否 Done / 检查有没有做完 / verify | **verify-done** | `Task(verifier)` → PASS/FAIL only |

**Default execution model (2026-07-16): single-lane serial.** At most **1** delivery leaf In Progress (1 worktree + 1 full pipeline). Do **not** spawn a second writer for another CE/slice while heavy gates (`mvn verify` / frontend gates / `docker-deploy-queue` / E2E) are in flight.

**Default when ambiguous but clearly delivery work:** treat as **deliver**
(`delivery-orchestrator`), not a clarifying menu — and **never** as multitask.

State one routing line before the first write:
`[routing] intent=<deliver|multitask-slices|deploy-queue|verify-done|…> → subagent=<…>`

## Mandatory first action (before edits)

Classify, then **invoke `Task` immediately** when matched.

**Delivery writes (default):** stage **0** `worktree-router` → provision `../DGE-<slice-id>` →
`move_agent_to_root` → then pipeline stages 1–13. **Never** implement on MAIN.

| Request class | First `subagent_type` | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Multi-step, full-stack, or ambiguous delivery | `delivery-orchestrator` | Starts at stage 0 worktree |
| **Any delivery / implement / fix (before first write)** | **`worktree-router`** | **Mandatory** unless read-only or `main-only` opt-out |
| Merge feature worktree + cleanup | `integration-merger` | Stage 11; after green gates |
| DOCX / PDF / LibreOffice / rendering module | `rendering-engineer` | Prefer over general backend |
| Backend behavior / Java / Flyway / runtime API | `backend-engineer` | After BDD if behavior-changing |
| Frontend behavior / Vue / Pinia / Playwright | `frontend-engineer` | E2E/UIUX follow |
| Behavior unclear or acceptance missing | `behavior-spec-author` | Blocks until confirmed |
| Plan phase / Task Master / COR-* status | `plan-orchestrator` | Single active phase + taskmaster |
| Requirements, PRD, matrix, API contract docs | `doc-keeper` | Before or with behavior code |
| Deep read-only audit (repo-wide) | `explore` | **Cursor built-in**; no project `.md` |
| Defect / PR review style scan | `bugbot` | **Cursor built-in**; optional |
| Code cleanliness / DRY / dead code | `code-quality-reviewer` | After architecture when both run |
| Build gates / Maven / pnpm / queued Docker | `build-deploy-agent` | **deploy-queue** intent |
| Complex rollback / multi-env release plan | `deploy-engineer` | Rollback planning only |
| Task slice complete | `post-task-doc-sync` | Before Done; on **main** if isolated |
| After doc sync (commit delegated) | `post-task-commit-review` | Honor `no-commit` / `no-push` |
| Claimed Done / pre-merge check | `verifier` | **verify-done** intent |

If multiple rows apply → **`delivery-orchestrator`** unless user named one specialist.

## Single-lane serial (default, 2026-07-16)

On this single Docker host, **parallel CE writers are retired as the default**:

- Always: `/worktree` + `git worktree add ../DGE-<slice-id>` + **`move_agent_to_root`** for the **one** active delivery session
- Queue next slices only after stage 11 merge + MAIN doc-sync of the current leaf
- Optional: next slice may author BDD / Red tests only (no verify / deploy / E2E overlap)
- Docker: only `.\scripts\docker-deploy-queue.ps1` (never a second stack)
- **`force-parallel` / `强制并行` only:** see `.cursor/skills/cursor-native-parallel/SKILL.md` (cap ≤2 writers; still queue Docker)

Slash commands remain available but are **not required**. Prefer `/deliver` over `/multitask-slices`.

## Parent MAY work inline only when

1. Read-only answer — no file writes.
2. Single mechanical edit (one typo/line) with no behavior/API/permission/plan change.
3. User opts out in the same message (`不要子 agent`).
4. Task enum lacks a new agent **and** the agent file documents an inline fallback
   (`worktree-router` / `integration-merger` / `verifier` only) — still follow that file’s rubric.

## Forbidden (parent)

- Asking the user to type `/deliver` / `/deploy-queue` / etc. when intent is already clear.
- Multi-file backend/frontend/rendering without the owning engineer.
- Plan/ledger/PRD/matrix updates without `doc-keeper` or `post-task-doc-sync`.
- Done without doc-sync (+ commit-review when commit in scope).
- Frontend Done without e2e-test-engineer + e2e-uiux-reviewer.
- Deep review via ad-hoc grep instead of `explore` / specialists.
- `generalPurpose` when a named specialist exists.
- Parallel `docker-deploy` / second compose project.
- Spawning a second delivery writer / CE leaf while another slice is In Progress (unless user `force-parallel`).
- Auto-mapping “继续做 / 把剩下的做完” to multitask — map to **serial deliver** of the sole-active queue head.
- Implementing delivery on MAIN without stage 0 worktree (`worktree-and-deploy-queue-constitution.mdc`).
- Running full build gates on MAIN while a feature worktree slice is active.
- Leaving feature worktrees after merge without `integration-merger`.

## Self-check (one line before first write)

`[routing] intent=<…> → subagent=<…> → reason=<…>`

## Supervisor mode

User stays in **one** parent session and speaks goals in natural language. Parent
autonomously maps intent → workflow → `Task` chain, synthesizes results, and continues
the next stage — no «要继续吗？」 or «请输入 /deliver» menus when direction is clear.

## Model selection

Fleet pin: `cursor-grok-4.5-high-fast` for every project specialist — see `.cursor/agents/MODEL-STRATEGY.md`.
**`inherit` forbidden.** Do not override `model` on Task unless the user explicitly requests a different slug.

